      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Leafs",
        "body": "The Toronto Maple Leafs didn't just open free agency - they detonated the division's goalie landscape with a bold, divisional gamble. <strong>Sergei Bobrovsky, a two-time Stanley Cup winner, has agreed to a three-year, $21M deal with the Leafs</strong>, instantly replacing Ryan Sheay and reshaping the back end of the roster. After a quiet 78-point season that left them 8th in the Atlantic, GM John Chayka declared, \"We got a lot done,\" as the club also added Colton Sissons, Jack Roslovic, Teddy Blueger, and Brandon Duhaime while trading Nick Robertson to Pittsburgh for a fourth-round pick. The 37-year-old Bobrovsky, now the new starting goalie, brings championship grit to a team hungry for stability. <strong>What to watch next: how Bobrovsky's presence elevates the Leafs' playoff ceiling and whether the depth signings can fill critical roster gaps</strong>.",
        "updated": "Updated July 2, 2026"
      },
