        "label": "What's Going On With the Jays",
        "body": "Toronto Blue Jays finally ripped the script on a sluggish Canada Day, turning a three-game Mets split into a statement win that echoes louder than the 11 games trailing them in the AL East. <strong>The Jays crushed the Mets 9-3</strong>, erupting with a 41-46 record and a solitary game win streak that suggests this team is still fighting for relevance despite sitting third in the division. Vladimir Guerrero Jr. is the quiet heartbeat of this resurgence, showing tangible signs of progress in that rout, even as the rotation remains a question mark. The bullpen imploded last week, but last night's offensive explosion offered a rare glimpse of contender energy. <strong>Saturday's 9:10 PM ET clash at Seattle against the Mariners</strong> will test whether this momentum is real or just a fleeting spark in a season that demands more consistency.",
